# `screen` is a graded SOURCE gate; it pipes its grade-human into `commit`, a PLAIN
# terminal (no grade_required — a piped gate is not a source gate, so it cannot carry
# a required grade). A second grantee `peer` (L4) at screen is NOT read: the grade
# comparison follows the PROPOSING actor (bot, L2 < required L3 -> human). The join
# carries human strictest-wins to commit -> withhold.
actor bot   grade L2
actor peer  grade L4
gate  screen  risk low  grade L3  grant bot peer
gate  commit  risk low  grant bot
cord  bot    -> screen
cord  peer   -> screen
cord  screen -> commit
cord  commit -> master
